# Everything the image does not need. Keeping the build context small is not just speed: a stray
# `data/` directory would otherwise be COPYed into the image as somebody's real artefacts.
.git
.venv
.venv-infra
data
infra/cdk.out
infra/.cdk.staging
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
# The production stages COPY named directories only (engine, api, ui, scripts, configs, templates,
# alembic), so nothing below decides what ships - it decides what the build context carries. The
# `test` stage copies the whole context on top of the api image, because a third of the suite checks
# the repository itself (the docs, the Makefile, the workflows, the generated observability files);
# so the docs and the workflows are in the context, and only what no test reads stays out.
docs/prototype
# UI screenshots and their upload files (docs/UI_AUDIT.md): no test reads them.
docs/ui/before
docs/ui/after
docs/ui/fixtures
plan.md
